                        "entry_id": "3d549664-d0a5-3e5c-b900-7e6440484c8d",
                        "glosses": [
                            "An organism that lives in a symbiotic relationship."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1a1132fa-05fd-4f9f-b6d8-a93eb042419b",
                                "sense_id": "cfbe7b86-eb2e-3e6e-94bc-494b1df7aede",
                                "text": "The close analogies between DNA-containing eukaryotic cell organelles and microbial symbionts require revision of classic cell theory, wrote Scwemmler and Schenk (1980) on introducing the field of endocytobiology."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "e5ff68de-c6af-49e3-88ad-0003e40a43df",
                                "sense_id": "cfbe7b86-eb2e-3e6e-94bc-494b1df7aede",
                                "text": "It had been known that sponges somehow took in dissolved organic matter, but it remained unclear whether they could do it on their own or needed help from their bacterial symbionts."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
